messages:
zoe: Heads up  onboarding spike: new users keep hitting import/runtime errors with the JS SDK. Quickstart only shows one snippet and it doesn't cover everyone.
liam: Can you paste the common errors?
zoe: Sure: "Named export 'InferenceClient' not found from '@redwood/inference'" and "TypeError: Cannot read property 'InferenceClient' of undefined" after `require()`. Also a couple of Bun/Deno reports.
maya: Sounds like classic default vs named + CJS/ESM mismatch. Bundlers and runtime flags (package.json type, tsconfig) change what consumers see.
liam: We should add an "Import patterns" micro-cheatsheet to quickstart and a tiny generator that creates the exact example for the user's environment (cjs/esm/ts/edge). Copy/paste reduces tickets.
zoe: Agreed. Draft cheatsheet I want in README (short, copy/paste):
```
// Node CommonJS (package.json WITHOUT "type": "module")
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new (Redwood.InferenceClient || Redwood.default?.InferenceClient)({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// Node ESM ("type": "module" or .mjs) - default import
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood.InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// Strict ESM / Edge runtimes (preferred for edge)
import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client2 = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// TypeScript (if you can't enable esModuleInterop)
import Redwood = require('@redwood/inference'); // fallback
const clientTs = new (Redwood as any).InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
```
liam: Also include a minimal tsconfig hint: `{ "compilerOptions": { "esModuleInterop": true, "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true } }`. That cuts early TS confusions.
maya: Add a tiny debug command set users/support can run to see how their runtime resolves the package: `node -e "console.log(require('@redwood/inference'))"` and in ESM shells `node -p "(await import('@redwood/inference'))"`.
support-bot: I'll add those commands to the support playbook so triage is faster.
build-eng: Operational note: we'll need an RFC to normalize publish artifacts. For now ensure package.json has `main` (CJS), `module` (ESM), and `types` keys and consider an `exports` map like: `{".":{"import":"./dist/esm/index.mjs","require":"./dist/cjs/index.cjs"}}`. Filing INF-342.
zoe: Short-term plan: 1) docs PR with the cheatsheet + four example apps (examples/js/{cjs,esm,ts,edge}); 2) small cli `rw-sdk-init` to scaffold the correct snippet for users during signup; 3) INF-342 to align builds.
liam: I like the CLI idea for onboarding flows. Could be a one-file generator that writes the right snippet into a starter project depending on `--target`.
maya: Also call out runtimes explicitly: Vercel Edge, Cloudflare Workers, Deno are ESM-only. Bun's module resolution can differ; include a note.
docs-bot: Draft PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/612  adds "JS SDK: Import patterns (CJS/ESM/TS/Edge)" section, example links, and a troubleshooting block. Please review.
zoe: Great. After docs land we'll update onboarding templates and support FAQ to point at the generator. That should reduce ticket volume. Closing this discussion for now.
